ng  olenna tyrell over so many iconic  characters but hear me out this is a  character that is old and is physically  not intimidating but she is still able  to be one of the biggest badasses in  game of thrones she's written with a  ferocious temperament and roasts  everyone she comes across not only is  her fierce and funny dialogue riveting  she's also a really smart character with  heaps of wisdom thanks to how much  experience she's gone through you may  think that elena talking about potential  love interest would be boring but from  elena's fun perspective of knocking down  and dismantling people with her quick  wit makes the dialogue significantly  better and this applies to every  dialogue scene she's in the only time  that she is matched is by tywin  lannister and even that scene was like a  fun fight where the future of their  houses were at stake and as a side point  i'm not accounting for the later seasons  but elena is really one of the only  characters that had a great scene which  was her confession to jaime that she  killed joffrey so not even david and dan  can ruin olenna  number 9  joffrey baratheon i feel like most  people would probably say that joffrey  is the best villain in the show but i  would argue that there's another main  villain that's even better joffrey on  his own is such an interesting case of  what if a child grows up into being the  worst human being possible that by  itself is a great what if scenario  character study but also pairing that  scenario with him becoming the king is a  jackpot idea it gives an evil character  unlimited power and plays into the  unpredictable menacing nature of a good  villain because he can literally do  anything listening to someone playing a  song adios tongue hanging out with sansa  time to shake up our relationship with a  nice crossbow joffrey's spontaneous  attitude and doing insane things on the  fly makes him an infectious villain to  watch and it's all grounded because this  is a spoiled c