tel can rival time when lannister in  a dialogue scene the sinister smiles  they give each other is cute as hell  oberyn is arguably the most likable  character in the show and it's a crime  that george rr martin killed him so  early it's a shame that we're getting  numerous spin-off shows from game of  thrones but we aren't getting an oberon  spin-off come on  pedro is selling his prime  number 13. ramsay bolton his  unpredictable nature makes him extremely  menacing and the amount of fury strikes  into his neighboring characters makes us  shudder in terror iwan rion does a  perfect job encapsulating ramsay for how  much of a twisted psychopath he is  the only reason i wouldn't put him a bit  higher is because the show really delves  into why ramsay turned out to be so  crazy we have one scene where he talks  about his mother briefly and up until  season six where his position is  challenged by ruse's new son we never  really get any conflicts between him and  ruse so it's a bit of a mystery why  ramsay's such a disturbed character  although to a degree it's fun to imagine  how dark his backstory is and the  vagueness behind it can aid him in a way  just in comparison to a fully fleshed  out villain like joffrey i would put  ramsay under him but i do think ewon  does some amazing legwork in his  performance to make ramsey such a crazy  villain and that paired with george rr  martin's diabolical writing it makes for  a great duo of a character  number 12  peter baelish the essence of what made  season 1 of game of thrones so great and  seasons 2 3 and 4 for that matter the  political and canifical nature of  littlefinger is very alluring and  entrancing we're always wondering and  theorizing what he's up to and trying to  figure out what his motives are is so  much fun the twist of him lying to ned  throughout season one imbues every later  scene with littlefinger with an essence  of doubt because we are always unsure of  whether he's lying or telling the truth  he's also a unique villain in that he's  always in the background manipulating  his story into different directions from  being the person that starts the war  between the lannisters and the starks to  killing lysa aaron and successfully  taking control of the veil also i think  the secret sauce of littlefinger is  aiden gillen's incredible rasping  grating voice it gives his character a  more creepy and unsettling demeanor and  it always sounds like he's 10 steps  ahead of everyone the amount of  confidence exuding from peter is  honestly sexy and i can't keep my eyes  off him whenever he's in the room  number 11  varus  so varys is very similar to littlefinger  in that they are both scheming  mysterious people who work behind the  scenes to achieve their own objective  the main difference is that varys is the  good guy or at least in the show the  primary reason i put him over  littlefinger is that his duo with tyrion  offers more in value than peter's duo  with sansa tyrion and varys's dialogue  scenes offer up some magnificent lines  and are a clear highlight in the first  few seasons littlefinger peaks higher  than varys in some iconic moments but  varys has a more consistent presence  since littlefinger is also traveling a  lot and doing things in the background  from that alone i think varus has more  to offer and his backstory is also more  intriguing because not only did a weird  pedo cut off his privates for fun but  there's also a magical aspect tied to it  in that when his privates were thrown  into the fire a voice called out thus  feeling varus's hatred towards magic and  making him a more detailed character  that and also the balance of sinisterism  and friendliness within varys makes him  even more curious as we try to figure  out what angle he's playing at his  ability to flip between those two states  reminds us that he's still a force to be  reckoned with and makes me respect him  even more  number 10  olenna tyrell  you may think i'm crazy for putting  olenna tyrell over so many iconic  characters but hear me out this is a  character that is old and is physically  not intimidating but she is still able  to be one of the biggest badasses in  game of thrones she's written with a  ferocious temperament and roasts  everyone she comes across not only is  her fierce and funny dialogue riveting  she's also a really smart character with  heaps of wisdom thanks to how much  experience she's gone through you may  think that elena talking about potential  love interest would be boring but from  elena's fun perspective of knocking down  and dismantling people with her quick  wit makes the dialogue significantly  better and this applies to every  dialogue scene she's in the only time  that she is matched is by tywin  lannister and even that scene was like a  fun fight where the future of their  houses were at stake and as a side point  i'm not accounting for the later seasons  but elena is really one of the only  characters that had a great scene which  was her confession to jaime that she  killed joffrey so not even david and dan  can ruin olenna  number 9  joffrey baratheon i feel like most  people would probably say that joffrey  is the best villain in the show but i  would argue that there's another main  villain that's even better joffrey on  his own is such an interesting case of  what if a child grows up into being the  worst human being possible that by  itself is a great what if scenario  character study but also pairing that  scenario with him becoming the king is a  jackpot idea it gives an evil character  unlimited power and plays into the  unpredictable menacing nature of a good  villain because he can literally do  anything listening to someone playing a  song adios tongue hanging out with sansa  time to shake up our relationship with a  nice crossbow joffrey's spontaneous  attitude and doing insane things on the  fly makes him an infectious villain to  watch and it's all grounded because this  is a spoiled child with an obscene  amount of power since joffrey's  backstory is more cemented and fully  realized in comparison to ramsay it  makes his clash with family members even  more tense and exciting like tywin  lannister being one of the best and  tyrion slapping him around never gets  old  number eight  daenerys targaryen  dany isn't in the top five what  but supercut's delight she's a main  character yes but for most of daenerys's  scenes she's generally dealing with the  same conflict tied to her being a  conqueror and that can get repetitive  when looking at her entire run however  is her conqueror and upbringing  character arc bad  no not by any means and it's extremely  entertaining her turn from being  suppressed and a scared child to a  raging leader with heaps of power is a  magnificent joy ride one of the most  iconic set-pieces in the whole show is  danny accumulating the unsullied and  from then on her story is intensely  riveting as she rolls through cities and  we get dopamine hit after dopamine hits  also in the rare cases where her  battle-hardened facade is peeled back in  a more dramatic scene like locking away  her dragons and ser jorah's betrayal i  think it offers a much-needed dose of  vulnerability although the most  interesting part of her entire arc to me  and concept is the mad queen arc but i  can't take that into account because it  was butchered later on so naturally i'll  put her under the other main characters  a bit because of the unfortunate  circumstance of one of the meatiest  parts of her story taking place during  season eight and seven and it also takes  a couple seasons for her character to  really pop off in comparison to tyrion  as an example who is amazing right out  of the gate  number seven  sandor clegane sandra clegane isn't just  a one trick funny dude who roasts people  left and right but he has a lot of  trauma under his heart exterior shell  and once you get to know him the hound  evolves into a more friendly puppy this  deconstruction is perfectly showcased  between the pairing of arya and the  hounds and their dialogue alone makes me  love him to death and this  deconstruction works both ways and that  the hound also challenges some of arya's  ideals and outlooks like what makes a  good warrior and the harsh reality of  the worlds he becomes her guardian and  this deserter turned father is one of my  favorite character arcs in the show and  i want to go back to him roasting people  because he has a miraculous town of  utterly disintegrating people with just  his usage of words it makes him even  more likeable when he's out here rolling  characters since he has no fear of death  but fire that's scary as hell and it's  also ironic that this brood of a  character is so scared of it it makes  his character even more vulnerable and  real not just an unstoppable force  number 6  jamie lannister  this man is at the center stage of one  of the best scenes in the whole show  where it's just a monologue about him  revealing the truth of the mad king and  exposing how being a knight isn't black  and white and is instead morally  complicated and throughout it's so  entrancing because we're impacting the  entirety to what makes this character  operate everything is spilling out and  it's beautiful i am describing one scene  out of a plethora but this is the magnum  opus that makes us love jaime as a  character before he came across as an  arrogant brat who thought he was always  in the right however through this  journey with brienne he learns what it  takes to be an upstanding knight george  r martin turns a seemingly irredeemable  killing machine into one of the most  relatable characters that feat alone is  some outstanding writing and jaime is  such a good character that he even  survives in later seasons until  obviously the one catastrophic line that  ruins his character obviously though i'm  not taking that into account the only  reason why i wouldn't put him higher on  my list was because he was kind of tied  to a post for a whole season and even  then there were still a couple great  dialogue scenes while he was a prisoner  number five arya stark  we made it to the top five and arya is  easily deserving i love her adventurous  and courageous attitude which makes her  seem even stronger when in the face of  death it's ironic how much bravery she  has given her young age which makes her  even more commendable also the overall  concept of a highborne lady wanting to  become a brilliant warrior is inherently  really intriguing and i think they fully  execute on that fun premise by her  joining the faceless assassins and also  training under syria pharrell her slowly  becoming more and more powerful over the  course of the series gives us a fun  progression and whenever she shows off  her new abilities and does something for  the first time we become enthralled that  and two of her seasons are spent hanging  out with the hound so she really has no  downtime and before that she had a  rollercoaster of a ride through king's  landing for season 1 in season 2 she  hung out with tywin most characters at  some point have a doll section in their  story but arya's storyline is always  delightful  number 4  cersei lannister  now this isn't the best villain that is  still yet to come cersei to me is a bit  more of a protagonist who occasionally  clashes with our main heroes on the  outside she may come across as hostile  however on the inside she's a loving  mother who will do anything for her own  children similar to catelyn although  cersei doesn't have a lot of honor to  hold her back this leads her to be more  vicious and seeing the link she goes to  for her children is crazy lena hidi also  thoroughly elevates the character with  her superb acting and seeing her hit her  extremes is breathtaking her singular  scene of the death of joffrey was  amazing and i'm really surprised she  didn't win any emmys for the entirety of  her run at cersei not only is she great  on her own but she also shines in  numerous character pairings whether  she's clashing with bobby b and ned  having chill talks with tyrion that  exposes her backstory her loving jaime  her desperately trying to impress her  father and rolling any other  miscellaneous character that crosses her  path  number 3  jon snow  going into this list i was going to  shaft jon because of how much the later  seasons made me hate him but after  rewatching some of the earlier seasons  i've come to like him a lot more again  and was reminded about how he was  actually a great character through the  first half of the show we don't just  have the same repetitive dialogue but a  character that's drowning in so much  conflict that tears him apart like his  constant state of friction with catelyn  him kind of being misled into thinking  the night's watch was a great place and  realizing everyone there are criminals  changing his entire outlook on life when  joining the free folk and balancing  helping them while simultaneously trying  to protect his brothers from getting  killed by the free folk jon snow changes  significantly throughout his journey  like he's doing 180s in almost every  season even through all this change dawn  is still anchored down by a strong  honorable core that is inherited from  ned so he's realistic while also having  a dynamic and thrilling story not to  mention that he led the episode the  watchers on the wall which is by far the  best episode in the show where jon is an  almighty warrior so not only is his  character development really good he's  also a really good fighter and his fight  scenes are really fun number two  tywin lannister  this is my list and i absolutely adore  tywin i hope you're proud of me for  refraining from putting him at number  one  charles dance perfectly sinks into the  character of tywin his voice is like  smooth jazz  that melts my insides the way he deals  with characters and destroys people in  such an easy manner makes me gush with  joy the scene in which he demolishes  joffrey by sending him to bed shows how  much of an alpha god he is tywin is the  best villain in the show not because of  his unpredictable or scary manner but  because of how much power the single man  has and from that power he literally has  the confidence of a lion just by staring  at you his eyes turn into daggers and a  single frown from this legend would be  like on the other end of a nuclear  explosion unlike some of the other  villains talwin has better dynamics with  other characters given that he isn't  flat out crazy joffrey and ramsey are  great on their own but generally they  close themselves off from getting too  close to anyone tywin on the other hand  is a father and he has to control his  children and that brings out a lot of  good dynamics and the best one is  definitely tyrion his hatred towards  tyrion slowly gets more and more  detailed until it explodes in season 4  with an ultimate showdown between them  this makes all of their interactions  engaging as hell and that is just one  dynamic out of a handful taiwan is bae  and it saddens me when i see lis eating  talent out of the top 10 in even 20.  number one  tyrion lannister  if you watch my videos this shouldn't be  that surprising because generally i gush  about how much i like him in season one  through four now if i was including the  entire show then i don't even know if  tyrion would make it onto my list from  how terribly stupid he became but hey  we're not looking at the bad baby we  gotta give our main characters a chance  so characters exclusive to the first few  seasons don't sweep the entire list  tyrion is the perfect storm of a  character he's funny smart brave  charismatic and despite having some of  these seemingly perfect characteristics  he still deals with a lot of conflict  and that he's always looked down on for  being a dwarf he's constantly fighting a  never-ending uphill battle and this  endless chain of conflict makes us love  him we get attached to characters who  are constantly at odds and are still  able to come out on top in large part  this is a thank you to him being a  lannister and that title also gives him  a massive confidence boost in scenes  where most people would be scared he's  still wittily talking his way out of  dangerous scenarios the ability to use  your words as a form of conflict  resolution is refreshing in a world  where so much conflict is resolved with  the swing of a sword tyrion doesn't need  one and that aspect makes him courageous  seeing him in any scene where he's being  challenged instantly makes it  entertaining because we are dying to see  how he outsmarts his opponents and even  when everyone is against him he is still  able to find a way to come out on top  like his outstanding trial by combat  speech i'm trying not to exceed that big  of a time limit for each of these  rankings but i could honestly go on for  a while about why tearing is the best  maybe i should just make it its own  video at this rate overall though his  journey throughout king's landing is  utterly riveting and to me he's the most  charming and likable character that i  love to watch any scene with tyrion is  amazing  i would go into honorable mentions to  argue why i didn't put some characters  on this list like theon and sansa being  two big ones but i think i'll delegate  that discussion to a pinned comment in  the comment section so if you're curious  you can look into that so you don't have  to sit through five minutes of me  defending myself regardless though thank  you for watching and let me know who  your favorite characters are down below
 

